    ],
    "matches": [
      0,
      2
    ],
    "comment": "IRS parity gap 2: the [+-]<n>(ms|s|m|h|d) relative-duration token round-trips as a plain literal — no special grammar — which is all sub-project #3 owns. Deliberately typed TEXT here rather than TIMESTAMP/duration: SearchExpressionParser never sees a column type (parseExpr takes no type argument), so the grammar/tree-shape point this case makes is identical regardless of the eventual column's type, and TEXT keeps this case clear of #4's (not-yet-landed) typed-value validation. Interpreting the digits+unit as an offset from request time, on an actual TIMESTAMP/duration column, is #1's and #4's job, not this parser's."
  },
